## 2. DAE Index Bound — Well-Posedness Guarantee

**Lemma 1 (Index-1 Guarantee).** Under three physically motivated conditions:

1. Dead-time is enforced between complementary switches (no shoot-through)
2. Leakage inductances Lₖ > 0 for all k
3. Capacitances C_in, C_out > 0

the switched DAE subsystem has index ≤ 1 in every switching mode σ.

**Proof:** The DAB electrical network, when ideal switches are replaced by their on-state resistances or open circuits, forms an RLC network with at least one capacitor or inductor in every loop and at every node. By the topological index theorem for electrical circuits (Estévez-Schwarz and Tischendorf, 2000), such networks yield DAEs of index at most 1. Conditions 1–3 ensure that no loop of pure voltage sources and no cut-set of pure current sources can form. Therefore consistent initial conditions always exist after every switching event and the continuous flow is uniquely determined by the initial condition and input trajectory. ∎

Index-1 is essential for the wireless system specifically because the coupling coefficient k_c varies with parking geometry — the DAE index must remain bounded regardless of this parametric variation to guarantee numerical tractability of the power control loop.

