## 10. Hybrid Phase-Shedding Supervisor

The UVCG contains N parallel DAB sub-modules. A hybrid automaton supervisor dynamically activates or deactivates sub-modules to maximise efficiency under the thermal safety constraint.

**Definition (Phase-Shedding Hybrid Automaton).** ℋ = (Q, X, Init, Flow, Jump, Guard, Reset) where:

- Discrete states Q = {q_k | k = 1,...,N}, with q_k representing exactly k active sub-modules
- Continuous state x = [z₁, z₂, P̂, Tj,1,...,Tj,N_dies]ᵀ
- Flow in location q_k governed by system (3.7), (3.9), (3.10) with per-phase loss coefficient βₖ > 0, strictly decreasing in k (fewer phases means higher per-phase current and faster heating)
- Guards: G_{k→k+1} = {x : Tj ≥ T_high} and G_{k→k-1} = {x : Tj ≤ T_low}
- Reset: identity map x⁺ = x⁻ (temperatures and electrical states are continuous across transitions)

The continuous thermal dynamics in location q_k are:

**Ṫj = −(1/Rth·Cth)·(Tj − T_amb) + (βₖ/Cth)·(z₁² + z₂²)**

where βₖ is strictly decreasing with k — this is the efficiency-thermal coupling: fewer active phases raises per-phase losses and heats junctions faster.

