## 13. Contract-Based Specification

All guarantees are encoded as assume-guarantee contracts in Signal Temporal Logic:

**Voltage Regulation Contract C_volt:**
Assumption: v_ref ∈ [300V, 900V], P ∈ [10kW, 350kW], |d(t)| ≤ d̄
Guarantee: □_{[0,∞)} (|v_o − v_ref| ≤ 0.01·v_ref) ∧ ◇_{[0,0.05]} □ (settled)
Formal basis: Theorem 1 (ISS) with γ ≤ 0.1 V/W

**Thermal Safety Contract C_therm:**
Assumption: T_amb ∈ [−20°C, 50°C], ΔT satisfies Theorem 2 condition
Guarantee: □_{[0,∞)} (Tj ≤ 125°C) ∧ ℙ(Tj > 120°C) ≤ 10⁻³
Formal basis: Theorem 2 (barrier certificate) + PCE-SMC validation

**Stability Contract C_stab:**
Assumption: P ∈ [10kW, 350kW], k_c ∈ [0.15, 0.40]
Guarantee: □_{[0,∞)} (phase_margin ≥ 45° ∧ gain_margin ≥ 6 dB)
Formal basis: ISS gain computation and small-gain theorem

**Compositional Verification Theorem:** The parallel composition of the backstepping controller M₁ and phase-shedding supervisor M₂ satisfies the system contract C_sys = C_volt ∧ C_therm ∧ C_stab, provided the compatibility conditions G_M2 ⊆ A_M1 and G_M1 ⊆ A_M2 hold — the ISS guarantee of M₁ bounds the electrical states that M₂ relies upon, and the thermal safety guarantee of M₂ bounds the parameter drift that M₁ relies upon.

