&= \dot{\alpha} - \frac{z_1}{C} - c_2 z_2 - \dot{\alpha} = -\frac{z_1}{C} - c_2 z_2.
\end{aligned}

So

\dot{z}_2 = -c_2 z_2 - \frac{1}{L C} z_1. \tag{E.3}

Adaptation law:

\dot{\hat{P}} = - \Gamma \frac{z_1}{v_o}, \quad \Gamma > 0. \tag{E.4}

Since P is constant, \dot{\tilde{P}} = \dot{\hat{P}}.

