\dot{z}_2 = -\frac{1}{L} z_1 - c_2 z_2.

From L \dot{z}_2 = u - v_o - L \dot{\alpha}, we set

u = v_o + L \dot{\alpha} - z_1 - c_2 L z_2. \tag{E.2-correct}

Then

L \dot{z}_2 = -z_1 - c_2 L z_2.

Now the derivative:

